<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly unchanged ahead of auction.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly unchanged ahead of auction.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were generally unchanged as traders awaited the results of the Treasury bill auction slated for later on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks are in a wait-and-see mode. We know that rates will go down further, but there's no consensus on how much lower they will go,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Only the one-week and two-month PHIBOR slipped marginally.</p>
<p>PHIBOR are the swap quotes compiled from 20 local and foreign banks operating in the country.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  JAN 10		 JAN 9</p>
<p>    1 W		10  3/8		 10  7/16</p>
<p>    2 W		10  5/16		10  5/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/4		 10  1/4</p>
<p>    2 M		10  3/8		 10  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/8		 10  3/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10  9/16		10  9/16</p>
<p>    12M		10 13/16		10 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		13-Jan		  10-Jan</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8938 Fax 8176267</p>
